Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: in the profiled models used on NFDI resources. Range schema:Review: all values are Review nodes.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://schema.org/Review" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/includedInDataCatalog">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">included in data catalog</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A data catalog which contains this dataset. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: in the profiled models used on data feeds. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: values are data portals, catalogues and databases.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/associatedMedia">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">associated media</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A media object that encodes this CreativeWork. This property is a synonym for encoding. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Added in version 0.3. CTO 3.0.0 types this property as owl:ObjectProperty without domain or range. Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: used on cto:CTO_0001005 (source item). Range schema:MediaObject, declared in CTO 3.0.0.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://schema.org/MediaObject" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/dataFeedElement">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data feed element</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
An item within a data feed. Data feeds may have many elements. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Added in version 0.3. CTO 3.0.0 types this property as owl:ObjectProperty without domain or range. Domain schema:DataFeed, declared in CTO 3.0.0. Range schema:DataFeedItem.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://schema.org/DataFeed" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://schema.org/DataFeedItem" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/item">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">item</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
An entity represented by an entry in a list or data feed (e.g. an 'artist' in a list of 'artists'). (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Added in version 0.3. Domain schema:DataFeedItem. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: the item is any entity the feed describes.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://schema.org/DataFeedItem" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/sameAs">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">same as</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
URL of a reference Web page that unambiguously indicates the item's identity. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: used on data portals, data feeds and schema:Role. Two ranges: rdfs:Resource for the plain IRI use (data portals, data feeds), and obo:BFO_0000001 (entity) since version 0.3 for Role nodes, which point to one of the 32 named role terms (typed schema:Role) in the CKG. Distinct from owl:sameAs.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/roleName">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">role name</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A role played, performed or filled by a person or organization. For example, the team of creators for a comic book might fill the roles named 'inker', 'penciller', and 'letterer'; or an athlete in a SportsTeam might play in the position named 'Quarterback'. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Used only on schema:Role. All values are xsd:string; in the CKG the string repeats the name of the role term the Role node points to with schema:sameAs (e.g. "Affiliation", "Author"). Added in version 0.3.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://schema.org/Role" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>

  <!--
           INVERSE PROPERTIES
           This version counts 1 inverse property.
           -->
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/member">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">member</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note of the inverse property:
A member of an Organization or a ProgramMembership. Organizations can be members of organizations; ProgramMembership is typically for individuals. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
This property is the inverse of schema:memberOf. RDFS cannot state the inverse relation, so it is declared separately without an axiom. Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: subjects are organisation, schema:Role, NFDI consortium and project. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: values are person, organisation, schema:Role and NFDI consortium. In the NFDI4Culture data the property is used twice in the path Organisation → schema:member → schema:Role → schema:member → Person.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>

  <!-- ===== nfdicore-range-extension.xml ===== -->
<!--
           Ranges for NFDIcore Properties used in the NFDI4Culture Application Profile
           RDFS Implementation, Version 0.1

           This document adds an rdfs:range to NFDIcore 3.0.0 properties that are used in the NFDI4Culture
           modelling but declared there without one. A property without a range cannot be followed by a
           class (or a literal) in a path, so the fields that use it cannot be completed in a path builder.

           Note that this is NOT a definition of these properties, which belong to NFDIcore. Ranges reflect
           NFDI4Culture usage only.

           Drafted by Delving, 5 November 2026, for review by George Bruseker (Takin.solutions)
           Namespace of the declared terms : https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/

           Contents:
           - 5 properties

           Encoding Rules:
           1. Only NFDIcore properties used in the NFDI4Culture modelling and declared without rdfs:range in
              NFDIcore 3.0.0 are listed. They keep their NFDIcore IRIs. Nothing else about them is repeated.

           2. Only rdfs:range is added. No rdfs:domain is added: in NFDIcore 3.0.0 these properties have no
              domain and so apply to any class, which is how the modelling uses them (scope obo:BFO_0000001).

           3. For the four inverse properties the range is the domain NFDIcore gives the forward property
              where it gives one (nfdicore:NFDI_0000191 "published by" has domain obo:IAO_0000030), else
              obo:BFO_0000001 (entity). nfdicore:NFDI_0010015 "has acronym" is an annotation property with
              string values and gets xsd:string.

           4. Scope notes quote the NFDIcore rdfs:comment; "Implementation note" records why the range is
              declared as it is.
           -->

  <!--
           PROPERTIES
           This version counts 5 properties.
           -->
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000113">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contact point of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
inverse of property "has contact point". (NFDIcore 3.0.0)

Implementation note:
Inverse of nfdicore:NFDI_0000112 "has contact point", which has range nfdicore:NFDI_0000102 (agent) and no domain. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: values are the resources, organisations and services the agent is a contact point of.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000117">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contributor of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
inverse of property "has contributor". (NFDIcore 3.0.0)

Implementation note:
Inverse of nfdicore:NFDI_0000116 "has contributor", which has range nfdicore:NFDI_0000102 (agent) and no domain. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0001028">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">creator of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
inverse of property "has creator". (NFDIcore 3.0.0)

Implementation note:
Inverse of nfdicore:NFDI_0001027 "has creator", which has range nfdicore:NFDI_0000102 (agent) and no domain. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class. NFDIcore 3.0.0 gives this property only a German-tagged label; the English label is supplied here.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000192">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">publisher of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
inverse of property "has publisher". (NFDIcore 3.0.0)

Implementation note:
Inverse of nfdicore:NFDI_0000191 "published by", which has domain obo:IAO_0000030 (information content entity) and range nfdicore:NFDI_0000102 (agent). Range obo:IAO_0000030.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://nfdi4culture.de/ontology/CTO_0001025">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is about real world entity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A provider URI (cto:source item) is about a real world entity, e.g. an instance of schema:Book, schema:Sculpture or nfdicore:Event. (CTO 3.0.0)

Implementation note:
CTO 3.0.0 ranges this property on the union of nfdicore:NFDI_0000004, nfdicore:NFDI_0000131, schema:Book, schema:LandmarksOrHistoricalBuildings, schema:Sculpture, schema:SheetMusic and schema:TheaterEvent. The CKG data mostly points to classes outside that union (mo:MusicalManifestation, schema:CreativeWork, schema:VisualArtwork, schema:ImageObject, schema:MusicEvent, schema:MusicComposition, crm:E34_Inscription, crm:E22_Human-Made_Object, cmif Letter), and the five schema.org classes are not placed in the BFO hierarchy. This file adds obo:BFO_0000001 (entity) as a range; the seven upstream ranges stay. Added in version 0.4 (George Bruseker, 6 November 2026).
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://nfdi4culture.de/ontology/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0010015">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has acronym</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A relation between an entity and its abbreviated form, representing a shortened version of the original term or phrase. (NFDIcore 3.0.0)

Implementation note:
An owl:AnnotationProperty in NFDIcore 3.0.0 with no range. Values are strings. Range xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/" />
  </rdf:Property>

  <!-- ===== rdfs-owl-extension.xml ===== -->
<!--
           BFO Terms for the NFDI4Culture Application Profile
           RDFS Implementation, Version 0.1

           This document declares, in RDFS, the Basic Formal Ontology term that the
           NFDI4Culture modelling uses as a field and that no loaded ontology declares with a domain:
           obo:BFO_0000050 (part of). Its purpose is to let this field be modelled without importing
           BFO as a whole. It is a bridging encoding with the least possible commitment.

           RDF Schema and OWL basics (rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, owl:sameAs) are not
           declared here: the platform's defaults vocabulary offers them on every class.

           Note that this is NOT a definition of the term. The scope note quotes its source; domain and
           range reflect NFDI4Culture usage only.

           Drafted by Delving, 5 November 2026, for review by George Bruseker (Takin.solutions)
           Namespace of the declared term : http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/

           Contents:
           - 1 property

           Encoding Rules:
           1. The term keeps its IRI. No subclass or subproperty relations are asserted.

           2. The domain and range are the top-level class obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), shared by NFDIcore
              and CTO, so the property can be used on any class.

           3. Scope notes are represented as rdfs:comment elements: "Scope note" quotes the source
              vocabulary, and "Implementation note" records how and why the term is declared as it is.
           -->

  <!--
           PROPERTIES
           This version counts 1 property.
           -->
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">part of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
a core relation that holds between a part and its whole (Basic Formal Ontology)

Implementation note:
Not included in the BFO subset that NFDIcore 3.0.0 imports. Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: used as the Part of field. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity).
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/" />
  </rdf:Property>
</rdf:RDF>
